Figure 5 illustrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, a dot plot, shows that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) alone results in minimal uptake, Nano-11 facilitates a substantial increase in both Nano-11 and OVA fluorescence within BMDCs when the antigen is adsorbed to it. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA, quantifies this effect, revealing a pronounced shift in fluorescence intensity for the Nano-11+OVA group, indicating a much greater antigen internalization by BMDCs. This demonstrates Nano-11's role in improving antigen delivery to DCs, a crucial step for initiating an effective immune response, as discussed in the surrounding text (Section 3.3).